.TH JITTERENTROPY-HASHTIME 1 2026-09-30 "jitterentropy x.y.z" "User Commands"
.\" groff re-enables hyphenation per paragraph unless HY is 0.
.nr HY 0
.nh
.SH NAME
jitterentropy-hashtime \- record raw noise data of the CPU Jitter RNG
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jitterentropy-hashtime
.I rounds repeats file
.RI [ option " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jitterentropy-hashtime
records the raw time deltas of the noise source of the CPU Jitter Random
Number Generator, before any conditioning - the data an SP800-90B entropy
assessment of the noise source takes.
.PP
It writes
.I rounds
time deltas, one decimal number per line, into each of the
.I repeats
files
.IR file \-0001.data,
.IR file \-0002.data
and so on. Every file is recorded on a collector of its own, allocated
anew, so that the files of one run are the rows of the SP800-90B restart
matrix.
.PP
The tool contains its own copy of the library and measures exactly the
code the library runs. The recordings are analyzed with the scripts in
.I tests/raw\-entropy
of the source distribution.
.SH OPTIONS
The first eight options set the
.B JENT_*
flag of the same name or field, described in
.BR jitterentropy (3).
Options are matched by their prefix.
.TP
.B \-\-ntg1
AIS 20/31 NTG.1 compliant operation
.RB ( JENT_NTG1 ).
.TP
.B \-\-force\-fips
FIPS 140 and SP800-90B compliant operation
.RB ( JENT_FORCE_FIPS ).
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-memory\-access
No memory access noise source
.RB ( JENT_DISABLE_MEMORY_ACCESS ).
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-internal\-timer
Never use the internal timer
.RB ( JENT_DISABLE_INTERNAL_TIMER ).
.TP
.B \-\-force\-internal\-timer
Use the internal timer instead of the hardware time stamp
.RB ( JENT_FORCE_INTERNAL_TIMER ).
.TP
.B \-\-all\-caches
Size the memory access region from all data caches
.RB ( JENT_CACHE_ALL ).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-mem " n"
Set the memory access region to 2^(\fIn\fR+9) bytes, with
.I n
from 1 (1 kB) to 20 (512 MB); 0 leaves the size to the library.
.TP
.BI \-\-hloopcnt " n"
Run 2^\fIn\fR hash loop iterations per measurement, with
.I n
from 0 to 7.
.TP
.BI \-\-osr " osr"
The oversampling rate; 0, the default, selects the minimum of 3.
.TP
.B \-\-hashloop
Record the hash loop alone, the first of the two NTG.1 noise sources,
instead of the common measurement.
.TP
.B \-\-memaccess
Record the memory access loop alone, the second NTG.1 noise source.
.TP
.BI \-\-loopcnt " n"
Run the recorded noise source with a loop count of
.I n
instead of the one the collector is configured with.
.TP
.BI \-\-cpu " n"
Pin the measurement to CPU
.IR n ,
on hybrid CPUs to record one core type at a time. Not available with the
internal timer, whose counting thread needs a CPU of its own, and only
where the platform can pin a thread.
.TP
.B \-\-e\-cores
Confine the measurement to the efficiency cores. macOS only.
.TP
.B \-\-p\-cores
Ask for the performance cores, a preference the scheduler may leave. macOS
only.
.BR \-\-cpu ,
.B \-\-e\-cores
and
.B \-\-p\-cores
are mutually exclusive.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print the status document of the collector the recording would use, and
record nothing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every file was recorded in full, 1 otherwise.
.SH EXAMPLES
The runtime data set and the restart data sets of an SP800-90B assessment:
.PP
.EX
jitterentropy-hashtime 1000000 1 jent\-raw\-noise
jitterentropy-hashtime 1000 1000 jent\-raw\-noise\-restart
.EE
.PP
The hash loop alone, in NTG.1 mode:
.PP
.EX
jitterentropy-hashtime 1000000 1 jent\-raw\-noise_hashloop \-\-ntg1 \-\-hashloop
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jitterentropy-flags (1),
.BR jitterentropy (3),
.BR jitterentropy-record (3)
